#
# libmali (mali_kbase): keep the GPU power domain up. The default policy,
# coarse_demand, drops the domain whenever the GPU idles; turning it back on
# sometimes gets no ack from the PMU ("failed to get ack on domain 'gpu'")
# and the next register write ends in an SError and a kernel panic, mid game
# (reports from two R35S/R36S, three panics on 2026-11-15/16). always_on
# costs about 10-20 mA with the launcher idle, less in a game, where the GPU
# is busy anyway. panfrost has no power_policy file and is left alone.
ACTION=="add|bind", SUBSYSTEM=="platform", DRIVER=="mali", TEST=="power_policy", ATTR{power_policy}="always_on"
